# Negotiation Deployment Authorization

- The project owner authorizes Codex to deploy, arm, disarm, and roll back
  negotiation strategy flags when live evidence warrants it, without requesting
  the same authorization again.
- Codex owns negotiation deployment decisions for this project. Use supported
  fleet tooling, explicit-zero rollbacks, and lossless live overlays.
- Never restart, signal, abandon, or interrupt live games merely to accelerate
  a rollout. Verify the exact configuration delta and subsequent live behavior.
- This authorization covers negotiation-owned configuration only. Preserve
  bargaining unless the user explicitly requests a bargaining change; also
  preserve persuasion, API keys, family topology, and unrelated fleet controls.
- Record consequential rollouts and reversions in `.ai/HANDOFF.md` with their
  evidence, boundary, affected slot, and verification.
- Higher-priority system, developer, repository-safety, and destructive-action
  constraints still apply. If one prevents deployment, report the conflict
  explicitly rather than claiming the change is live.
